  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off on June 15th and an initial budget of $500,000. The project has secured a strategic partnership with TechInnovate for AI research. Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase and the prototype for secure file sharing, which was tested ahead of schedule. The team has expanded to include Mike Chen (machine learning) and Lisa Ray (cloud computing). Following the design phase, the project is moving into development under lead developer Omar Jensen. A total budget of $2M has been approved by the executive board, with detailed allocations to be discussed on August 1st. The next phase involves user interface enhancements starting in October, and feedback on the prototype is being sought by the end of November. A celebration for the testing milestone is scheduled for October 10th."
